// VS Code: read a kernel tree through clangd, not through cpptools IntelliSense.
//
// cpptools does not read ~/.config/clangd/config.yaml, and on a GCC-built kernel
// its own parser reports hundreds of errors that no build ever produced.  The
// clangd extension is the same clangd Neovim runs, so it picks up the per-tree
// blocks `kbuildlab tags` writes and reaches the same near-zero diagnostic count.
//
// Merge into ~/.config/Code/User/settings.json.  cpptools keeps its debugger;
// only its parser is switched off.
//
// No -j here on purpose: VS Code settings cannot compute one, and a number that
// is right on one machine is wrong on the next.  clangd defaults to the host's
// thread count, and --background-index-priority keeps it out of the way.
{
    "C_Cpp.intelliSenseEngine": "disabled",
    "clangd.arguments": [
        "--background-index",
        "--clang-tidy",
        "--completion-style=detailed",
        "--header-insertion=never",
        "--pch-storage=disk",
        "--background-index-priority=background",
        "--limit-results=200",
        "--limit-references=2000"
    ]
}
